Package: mcp-server-patreon
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 python3-dotenv (>= 1.0),
 python3-fastmcp (>= 4.1.4),
 python3-httpx (>= 0.28),
 python3-pydantic (>= 2.7),
Provides: patreon-mcp-server
Description: MCP server for the Patreon API over stdio
 Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that gives an LLM agent read-only
 access to the Patreon API v2: the authenticated user's identity, the
 creator's campaigns with tiers, campaign members (patrons) and posts,
 with cursor-based pagination.
 .
 Runs over stdio. The Patreon creator access token is read from the
 PATREON_ACCESS_TOKEN environment variable and is never a tool
 parameter; patron e-mail addresses are not fetched. Ships the mcprack
 environment-variable manifest at
 /usr/share/mcp-server-patreon/server.json; the upstream binary name
 patreon-mcp-server is also installed.

Package: mcprack-mcp-server-patreon
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 mcprack (>= 1.5.4),
 mcp-server-patreon (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: Registers Patreon MCP server into mcprack catalog
 Companion package for mcp-server-patreon. Installing it registers
 the mcp-server-patreon binary as an available MCP server in the local
 mcprack instance; removing it unregisters it again.
